  "area": "compose",
  "description": "AGSC-07-26: the order of the survivors in `brief.json` (`order`). Expected values are derived by hand from the rule: a member comes after the targets of its `requires`, `broader` and `derived-from` edges (authored or computed), and among the members all of whose predecessors are taken the least slug by code point goes next. `precedence-then-code-point`: `alpha` is free and least, so it is first; then `lib`, the least of the free members `lib`, `root`, `source-note` and `zeta`, which frees `app`; then `app`, `root` (which frees `leaf`), `leaf`, `source-note` (which frees `report`), `report` and `zeta`. `the-input-order-does-not-reach-the-order` gives the same selection reversed and expects the same order (AGSC-07-09). `a-cycle-across-two-keys-takes-the-least-slug`: `x` derived-from `y` puts `y` first and `y` broader `x` puts `x` first, a cycle through two keys that AGSC-03-07 and AGSC-03-08 do not refuse; `z` is free and goes first, then no member is available, so the least slug left, `x`, is taken, then `y`. The phrase of the plan is dependency order, not a reading order.",
